=====================================================================
Enhancements to the PALASM 4 Online Help System
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Navigating between ERROR RECOVERY, LANGUAGE REFERENCE, and INDEX OF TOPICS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Navigating between online applications no longer requires that you return
to PALASM 4.

- From LANGUAGE REFERENCE and INDEX
   1. Select "Navigate" from the menu bar.
   2. Select the desired online application from the pull-down menu.




- From ERROR RECOVERY
   1. Select "Other" from the menu bar.
   2. Select "Navigate" from the new menu bar.
   3. Select the desired online application from the pull-down menu.

Viewing other documents from within the ERROR RECOVERY online application
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
You can now view, in read-only mode, the following files generated by
PALASM 4 during compilation or simulation: the fitter report (Mach designs
only), the simulation history file, and the simulation trace report.

You can also view any text document in any disk drive installed on your
system, by selecting the desired drive, directory, and filename from a
specialized menu.


- Viewing a PALASM 4 file
   1. Select "Other" from the menu bar.
   2. Select "View" from the new menu bar.
   3. Select "Fitter Report," "Simulation History," or "Simulation Trace"
      from the pull-down menu.

- Viewing any other text file
   1. Select "Other" from the menu bar.
   2. Select "View" from the new menu bar.
   3. Select "Other File," from the pull-down menu.
   4. Use the menu shown below to select the desired file from any
      directory on any disk drive.  If you have a mouse, you can
      double-click on the desired filename.  From the keyboard, use
      the up and down arrows to move within a list.  Use the Tab key
      to move from list to list or to highlight the "Ok" and "Cancel"
      buttons.  Press return to make your selection.
